{"strongs": "H3336", "word": "יֵ֫צָר", "translit": "ye.tser", "root": "יצר", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "form, framing, purpose", "definition": "I. יֵ֫צָר noun masculine Isa 26:3 form, framing, purpose ; — ׳ י Gen 6:5 + 5 t.; יִצְדוֺ Deut 31:21 ; Hab 2:18 יִצְרֵנוּ Ps 103:14 — 1. pottery , formed by the potter Isa 29:16 . 2. form of a graven image Hab 2:18 . 3. form of man as made of the dust Psalm Hab 103:14 . 4. of what is framed in the mind (compare יָצַר 1 c, 2 b ), imagination, device, purpose: יצר מחשׁב(ו)ת לב(בׅ Gen 6:5 ( J ), 1Chr 29:18 מחשׁבות ׳ י 1Chr 28:9 לב ׳ י Gen 8:21 ( J ); יֵצֶר alone Deut 31:21 ( J ); יֵצֶר סָמוּךְ Isa 26:3 a stedfast purpose (or frame of mind). (In Late Hebrew יֵצֶר is common in sense of impulse: יצר הטוב and יצר הרע of good and bad tendency in man.)", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3676')\">BDB3676</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3336')\">H3336</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3675')\">BDB3675</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3677')\">BDB3677</entry></div><p> I. <bdbheb>יֵ֫צָר</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Isa 26:3\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(23,26,3)\">Isa 26:3</ref></sup> <highlightword>form, framing, purpose</highlightword>; — <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 6:5\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(1,6,5)\">Gen 6:5</ref> + 5 t.; <bdbheb>יִצְדוֺ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 31:21\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(5,31,21)\">Deut 31:21</ref>; <ref ref=\"Hab 2:18\" b=\"35\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(35,2,18)\">Hab 2:18</ref> <bdbheb>יִצְרֵנוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 103:14\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"103\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"103\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(19,103,14)\">Ps 103:14</ref> — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>pottery</highlight>, formed by the potter <ref ref=\"Isa 29:16\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"29\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"29\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(23,29,16)\">Isa 29:16</ref>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> form of a graven image <ref ref=\"Hab 2:18\" b=\"35\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(35,2,18)\">Hab 2:18</ref>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>3.</b> form of man as made of the dust Psalm <checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"Hab 103:14\" b=\"35\" cBegin=\"103\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"103\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(35,103,14)\">Hab 103:14</ref>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>4.</b> of what is framed in the mind (compare <bdbheb>יָצַר</bdbheb> <b>1 c, 2 b</b>), <highlight>imagination, device, purpose:</highlight> <bdbheb>יצר מחשׁב(ו)ת לב(בׅ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 6:5\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(1,6,5)\">Gen 6:5</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"1Chr 29:18\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"29\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"29\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(13,29,18)\">1Chr 29:18</ref> <bdbheb>מחשׁבות</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Chr 28:9\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(13,28,9)\">1Chr 28:9</ref> <bdbheb>לב</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 8:21\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(1,8,21)\">Gen 8:21</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>); <bdbheb>יֵצֶר</bdbheb> alone <ref ref=\"Deut 31:21\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(5,31,21)\">Deut 31:21</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>); <bdbheb>יֵצֶר סָמוּךְ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 26:3\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(23,26,3)\">Isa 26:3</ref> a <highlight>stedfast purpose</highlight> (or <highlight>frame</highlight> of mind). (In Late Hebrew <bdbheb>יֵצֶר</bdbheb> is common i